#: umbriel-docs:actions
msgid "Actions are the compositor's verbs. Bind one under `[keybinds]`, attach it to a hot corner, or run it with `umbriel msg <action>`. `umbriel msg --help` prints this same list, with the same wording and the same grouping. See Keybinds for chord syntax and IPC for the socket behind `umbriel msg`, including the event stream that reports what an action changed."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:animation
msgid "Animation settings live under `[animation]`. The top-level values provide defaults, and each event can override them."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:appearance
msgid "Configure Umbriel's colors, window decorations, blur, and shadows."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:configuration
msgid "The packaged starting configuration is `examples/config.toml`. Copy it before making local changes:"
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:effects
msgid "Effects are GLSL programs Umbriel runs on animation events, on the focused window's border, on windows, on whole outputs, and around the pointer. Every effect is off until you select one. Umbriel ships a small set; each is a preset you include and then name where it should apply."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:index
msgid "Umbriel is a Wayland compositor with scrolling and tiling layouts, independent workspaces per monitor, and configurable visual effects. It works on its own or with Noctalia, a desktop shell designed to integrate with Umbriel."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:input
msgid "Configure keyboard, pointer, touchpad, tablet, cursor, and focus behavior under `[input]`."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:installation
msgid "Umbriel is packaged for several Linux distributions. Prefer a distribution package when one is available; it provides the simplest installation and upgrade path."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:ipc
msgid "Umbriel exposes a local UNIX socket for queries, actions, and event subscriptions. Most users should use the `umbriel` command rather than connect to the socket directly."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:keybinds
msgid "Configure bindings under `[keybinds]`. See Actions for the complete action list."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:layer-rules
msgid "Layer rules apply visual effects to layer-shell surfaces such as bars, launchers, and notifications. Run `umbriel layers` to list active namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:layout
msgid "Choose one layout mode for each workspace. Configure the default globally, then use workspace rules for exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:outputs
msgid "Output sections configure monitors by connector name, such as `DP-1`, or by monitor identity:"
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:scratchpad
msgid "A scratchpad stores windows outside normal workspaces so they can be shown or hidden quickly. Its windows float and appear together."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:security
msgid "Umbriel keeps the current desktop visible while an `ext-session-lock-v1` client prepares a mapped lock surface for every active output. The client has up to three seconds to provide those surfaces. Umbriel then switches every output to the lock scene and reports the session as locked only after each active output has presented a secure frame."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:streaming
msgid "Sunshine streams a desktop to Moonlight clients. Pointed at a virtual output, it streams a monitor that exists only for the session, at the client's resolution and frame rate, while the physical monitors keep their layout."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:window-rules
msgid "Window rules apply settings to matching applications. Every matching rule contributes its values; when two set the same field, the later rule wins."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:workspaces
msgid "Each output has its own workspaces. Choose a dynamic or fixed model, then use workspace rules to customize individual entries."
msgstr ""

#: umbriel-docs:workspaces-overview
msgid "The overview displays every workspace and lets you navigate, focus, close, and move windows."
msgstr ""
